\ Rung 7: the outer interpreter is one primitive, INTERPRET, as in jonesforth.
: SQUARE DUP * ;
5 SQUARE . CR
\ A word that is neither defined nor a number is a parse error.
SQAURE
\ WORD reads the next name and TELL prints it.  WORD's buffer is reused by
\ the interpreter's own WORD, so both run inside one definition.
: ECHO WORD TELL ;
ECHO hello CR
\ CHAR gives the first byte of the next word.
CHAR A . CHAR z EMIT CR
\ ' inside a definition gives an execution token for EXECUTE.
: TICK-SQUARE ' SQUARE ;
6 TICK-SQUARE EXECUTE . CR
\ QUIT empties the return stack (R0 RSP!) before each word: it holds no
\ return addresses at the top level, and one inside a word.
: RDEPTH R0 RSP@ - ;
R0 RSP@ - . RDEPTH . CR
